\title{iCARE: Individualized Coherent Absolute Risk Estimation}
\description{
iCARE builds, applies and validates models for the absolute risk of a
disease. An absolute risk model combines
\enumerate{
\item a model for the \strong{relative risks} of the risk factors, typically
estimated in a cohort or case-control study,
\item a \strong{reference dataset} of risk factors representing the population in
which the model is applied,
\item the population's age-specific \strong{disease incidence rates}, and
\item optionally, age-specific rates of \strong{competing mortality}.
}

The main functions are
\itemize{
\item \code{\link[=computeAbsoluteRisk]{computeAbsoluteRisk()}}: estimate absolute risks for covariate and/or
SNP profiles, including profiles with missing risk factors;
\item \code{\link[=computeAbsoluteRiskSplitInterval]{computeAbsoluteRiskSplitInterval()}}: the same when the relative-risk
model or the risk-factor distribution changes at a cut age;
\item \code{\link[=ModelValidation]{ModelValidation()}}: validate a model in a cohort or nested
case-control study (calibration and discrimination);
\item \code{\link[=plotModelValidation]{plotModelValidation()}}: publication-ready figures of a validation.
}
}
